@INVARIANT VERDICTS (11 checked). VERIFIED CORRECT (7), recorded as proven so a later cycle need not redo them: DCE walks backward from root-end via stack.pop() (LIFO/DFS not BFS), unreachable nodes emit no GLSL and consume no slots, empty active set returns the identity body; disabled nodes still emit the propagation triple from in1 but skip def.glsl and consume no slots; the distOverride window is exactly (-1.0, 999.0) with v_start_d seeded to 1000.0; param overflow degrades silently with the compiler emitting the literal and setP dropping writes (minor nuance: condition slots fall back to '2.0'/'0.0', not just '0.0'); topologicalSort's tie-break is alphabetical via queue.sort() before each shift, so compile order is deterministic across runs; the nodes.find inside the loop is O(N^2); and isStructureEqual compares exactly id/type/enabled/JSON.stringify(bindings)/condition.active, deliberately excluding condition.mod, condition.rem and params so slider retuning does not recompile. hasCycle's algorithm itself is sound (the recStack.delete outside the visited guard is a harmless no-op). FALSIFIED (4): the getParam-order invariant, the 'THREE places' root count, the 'store calls hasCycle' claim, and by omission isStructureEqual's silence about edges.

GUARD HEALTH — the headline. This subsystem has ZERO executable coverage. Not thin, zero. compileGraph, updateModularUniforms, topologicalSort, hasCycle and isStructureEqual are never invoked by any npm script, proven by falsification plus source. That is why both real bugs sat here undetected and why both came back as Tier V. The whole path is pure functions with no WebGL dependency, so a node-only harness would be cheap and is the single highest-value follow-up from this subsystem.

NOT REACHED: (a) the `else if (contentChanged)` branch of setGraph emits CONFIG with {pipeline} only, no graph, while MaterialController.syncModularUniforms takes (pipeline, edges) and defaults edges to []. If ConfigManager does not retain the previous graph, that path could pack uniforms against an empty edge set — which changes DCE liveness and therefore slot layout. Not traced, not claimed; a concrete thread for whoever owns the renderer rule. (b) Node id uniqueness across save/load — NodeRegistry.register does a bare Map.set with no duplicate check. (c) The remaining ~21 node definitions were checked only for getParam/inputs parity, not GLSL correctness.
